{"diagnosis": "Loopback TX of 0xa5 was received as 0xfc (TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xfc want 0xa5, tohost FAIL 0xdead). ser_tx is driven as send_pattern[0] per line 107, but line 131 shifts as {1'b1, send_pattern[9:2]} which drops two bits per tick and builds a 9-bit value, corrupting the serial stream. Root cause is the [9:2] slice; correct single-bit shift is [9:1] to preserve data and stop-bit 1s.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
 			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
-				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:2]};
+				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (FAIL 0xdead cleared), uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

